WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.088
StatePort starts with named applications, not a blank chat. This private-alpha fixture shows ongoing work with its own purpose, durable state, decisions, and history.

00:00:11.538 --> 00:00:23.874
The application plane provides purpose and continuity. StatePort owns intent, authority, canonical state, evidence, and acceptance. Those facts do not belong to an agent session.

00:00:24.338 --> 00:00:37.106
Conversation is one view inside the application. The execution plane is separate: the harness runs an authorized task and returns observations and candidate output, but it does not own accepted state.

00:00:37.571 --> 00:00:49.259
The source view says whether an application source is verified. A development candidate can provide isolated-test evidence, but it does not silently become a canonical release or production install.

00:00:49.709 --> 00:00:57.989
The same application list remains readable on a small screen. This is a local interface view, not evidence of a separate mobile release.

00:00:58.443 --> 00:01:10.083
This private alpha has one exercised provider path: Codex in supervised-direct mode. Other providers are not qualified by this walkthrough, and there is no public software download yet.
